<title>HONG KONG: HK Feb orders on hand fall nine pct yr on yr.</title>
<headline>HK Feb orders on hand fall nine pct yr on yr.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Census and Statistics Department said February orders-on-hand fell nine percent in value on the year against a seven percent drop in January.</p>
<p>The following are provisional percentage changes in the</p>
<p>value of orders-on-hand in February 1997 over February 1996 (*</p>
<p>means that comparative figure has been revised and *** means</p>
<p>that the change is within +/- 0.5 percent):</p>
<p>						   Feb 1997   Jan 1997</p>
<p> All industries covered in the survey    -9	   -7</p>
<p> Wearing apparel				 -5	   -5</p>
<p> Textiles					  -8	   -9</p>
<p>						   Feb 1997   Jan 1997</p>
<p> Electronic Products			  -14	  -11</p>
<p> Electrical products			   -4	  ***(*)</p>
<p> Fabricated metal products		   +4	  +10</p>
<p> Plastic products			     -21	  -20(*)</p>
<p> Printing and publishing		     -3	   -2(*)</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
